      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Aggressive antitrust action against big tech stifles the very innovation that drives modern progress. These massive platforms benefit from network effects, which allows them to invest billions in R&D that smaller companies simply cannot match. Breaking them up would fragment these ecosystems, leading to a less seamless and less innovative user experience for everyone. Therefore, the focus should be on fostering competition through market dynamics, not through heavy-handed government intervention.",
